  "desc": "Panorama of Innichen (called San Candido by Italian) in South Tyrol, Italy. Part of a series of 32 paintings executed by Valentin Gappnigg between 1698 and 1702. Gappnigg had been commissioned by the prince-bishop of Freising, Johann Franz Eckher von Kapfing und Liechteneck, to paint views of the various possessions of the prince-bishopric. While the core territories of Freising were located in Bavaria, it also included several far-flung enclaves located inside Tyrol, Styria, Carinthia, Upper Austria and Carniola (now Slovenia).",
